    {
        "Id": 98,
        "ActionId": 98,
        "Type": 301,
        "Params": [
            "",
            "Asimov",
            "I'll send you a detailed report later, but put simply, Amalgamation technology is a bridge connecting individual M.I.N.D.s. Its ultimate objective is to construct a vast consciousness network: the Amalgamation array.",
            2
        ]
    },
    {
        "Id": 99,
        "ActionId": 99,
        "Type": 204,
        "Params": [
            1,
            12
        ]
    },
    {
        "Id": 100,
        "ActionId": 100,
        "Type": 301,
        "Params": [
            "",
            "Mina",
            "I saw that much firsthand. Everyone linked gets a massive power boost... even starts using tech they shouldn't understand.",
            1
        ]
    },
    {
        "Id": 101,
        "ActionId": 101,
        "Type": 301,
        "Params": [
            "",
            "Asimov",
            "It's not just enhancement. It is completion. We previously misidentified the instability in the Arctic Route Union's humanoid-hybrid M.I.N.D.s as a flaw. In reality, it was a deliberate design gap.",
            2
        ]
    },
    {
        "Id": 102,
        "ActionId": 102,
        "Type": 204,
        "Params": [
            1,
            4
        ]
    },
    {
        "Id": 103,
        "ActionId": 103,
        "Type": 301,
        "Params": [
            "",
            "Mina",
            "Are you saying they engineered humanoid-hybrids specifically for Amalgamation?",
            1
        ]
    },
    {
        "Id": 104,
        "ActionId": 104,
        "Type": 301,
        "Params": [
            "",
            "Asimov",
            "Correct. Bionic machines possess dedicated Amalgamation access points. Non-humanoid collectives induce M.I.N.D. instability, but these perceived defects perfectly complement Amalgamation's requirements.",
            2
        ]
    },
    {
        "Id": 105,
        "ActionId": 105,
        "Type": 301,
        "Params": [
            "",
            "Asimov",
            "The technology's purpose is to construct a macro-array from countless individual nodes, recalibrating each unique entity—from individual to collective, and back again.",
            2
        ]
    },
    {
        "Id": 106,
        "ActionId": 106,
        "Type": 301,
        "Params": [
            "",
            "Mina",
            "So after the Amalgamation, they become \"complete\"... That explains the historical obsession with perfecting humanoid-hybrid frames.",
            1
        ]
    },
    {
        "Id": 107,
        "ActionId": 107,
        "Type": 306,
        "Params": [
            1
        ]
    },
    {
        "Id": 108,
        "ActionId": 108,
        "Type": 204,
        "Params": [
            1,
            3
        ]
    },
    {
        "Id": 109,
        "ActionId": 109,
        "Type": 301,
        "Params": [
            "",
            "",
            "\"Ultimate Amalgamator Malkuth\"—a term Mina recalls from the manuscript during her talk with Asimov. This, she now understands, is the key. \"Complete\" doesn't just mean the Amalgamator is finished; it means the entire system, including its subordinate frames, is now whole."
        ]
    },
    {
        "Id": 110,
        "ActionId": 110,
        "Type": 306,
        "Params": [
            0
        ]
    },
    {
        "Id": 111,
